# Trust roots — the single source of truth.
#
# Every path below can change what CI runs, what it trusts, or what the
# toolchain and gates accept; a change to any of them needs the code owner's
# review. The same file is read by `.github/ci/trust_roots.py`, which drives
# the `trust-root-diff` check and the `verify-manifest.py` trust-root check,
# so this list is never hand-synced anywhere else.
#
# Accepted subset (anything else is refused by `trust_roots.py`):
#   - one pattern plus owners per line; every rule has the SAME owner set,
#     so GitHub's last-match-wins ordering can never un-own a path;
#   - a pattern containing `/` starts with `/` (anchored at the repo root);
#     a pattern without `/` is one path component matched at any depth;
#   - a trailing `/` (or `/**`) means "this directory and everything in it";
#   - `*` and `?` match within one component; no `[`, `!`, `\`, inline `#`;
#   - every rule matches at least one tracked file.

# CI definitions, actions, gate SSOTs, and this file.
/.github/                                       @arthurmaciel
# nextest profiles and release-please configuration.
/.config/                                       @arthurmaciel
# Build, gate, and index tooling run by CI.
/tools/                                         @arthurmaciel

# Cargo configuration, manifests, lockfiles, and build scripts at any depth.
.cargo                                          @arthurmaciel
Cargo.toml                                      @arthurmaciel
Cargo.lock                                      @arthurmaciel
build.rs                                        @arthurmaciel

# Toolchain pin and lint/format policy.
rust-toolchain*                                 @arthurmaciel
clippy.toml                                     @arthurmaciel
rustfmt.toml                                    @arthurmaciel
/deny.toml                                      @arthurmaciel

# Install entry point and the governance documents gates enforce.
/install.sh                                     @arthurmaciel
/PRINCIPLES.md                                  @arthurmaciel
/AGENTS.md                                      @arthurmaciel

# Scripts CI runs from outside the tooling tree (`verify-manifest.py` check 12
# refuses a CI-run script that no rule here owns).
/editors/tests/                                 @arthurmaciel
/editors/tree-sitter-ipe/scripts/               @arthurmaciel
/tests/fixtures/admission/                      @arthurmaciel

# Byte-exact goldens: the reference output every emit test compares against.
/tests/golden/                                  @arthurmaciel
/src/ipe-cli/tests/golden/                      @arthurmaciel
/src/ipe-cli/tests/g_*/                         @arthurmaciel
/src/compiler/diagnostics/tests/render_goldens/ @arthurmaciel
